The utility displays a series of characters that first clears the
hardware terminal tab settings and then initializes the tab stops
at  the  specified  positions  and optionally adjusts the margin.
The phrase "tab‐stop position N" means that, from the start of  a
line  of output, tabbing to position N shall cause the next char‐
acter output to be in the (N+1)th column on that line.  The  fol‐
lowing options are supported: Specifies repetitive tab stops sep‐
